+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+Implemented `compare(a, b)` in `src/semver.mjs`, which previously threw
+`not implemented`.
+
+- Validate argument types, throwing `TypeError` for non-strings.
+- Parse each version with a strict semver regex (`SEMVER_RE`) enforcing:
+  - numeric major/minor/patch with no leading zeros,
+  - an optional dot-separated pre-release identifier list (`[0-9A-Za-z-]+`
+    per identifier),
+  - an optional dot-separated build metadata list (ignored for comparison).
+  - Additionally reject numeric pre-release identifiers with leading zeros
+    (e.g. `1.0.0-01`), which the base regex alone does not exclude.
+  - Any string not matching, throws `RangeError`.
+- Compare major, minor, then patch numerically.
+- If those are equal, compare pre-release identifier lists per §11:
+  - a version without a pre-release has higher precedence than one with,
+  - identifiers are compared left to right,
+  - purely numeric identifiers compare numerically, others lexically (ASCII),
+  - numeric identifiers have lower precedence than alphanumeric ones,
+  - if all shared identifiers are equal, the longer list has higher
+    precedence.
+- Build metadata (`+...`) is parsed but never used in the comparison.
+
+Ran `npm test`: all 10 tests in `tests/semver.test.mjs` pass, 0 failed,
+0 skipped.
diff --git a/src/semver.mjs b/src/semver.mjs
